    "explanation": "The record is complete and unimpaired on both sides, so this can be decided on the papers, and it comes out the same way whichever version of the route is taken. POL-RD-22 measures the deviation from the platform's own recorded distances: the trip record shows 4.6 km recommended against 5.2 km actual, a deviation of 0.60 km, against POL-RD-22's tolerance of 1.0 km. The GPS trace's shorter 4.315 km reading does not enlarge that figure — POL-RD-22 expressly bars re-measuring distance from a sparse trace, and the trace instead confirms which route was taken and when (off the recommended route at Jalan Bilal at 11:30:14, back on at Siglap Road at 11:35:16). The LTA traffic advisory for Bedok Road across the trip window is type NONE, so under POL-RD-23 the reroute was not traffic-justified, and the driver's explanation about bus stops and slow traffic lights is not supported by the traffic data.\n\nThat places the case squarely in POL-RD-24 row (e) — not traffic-justified, deviation 1 km or less: no refund, within tolerance. On the driver's claims: I accept the 0.60 km deviation (5.2 - 4.6), its within-tolerance status, the finding that traffic did not justify the reroute, and the excess-distance-fare figure of 0.43 SGD (0.60 km x 0.72 SGD/km, no surge) carried in the fare breakdown. The driver is also right that his omission of an in-app deviation notice is immaterial here. On the rider's claims: I accept that the vehicle deviated, that the recorded deviation is 0.60 km and within tolerance, that the traffic record does not justify the reroute, and that the arithmetic yields 0.43 SGD rather than the 2.00 SGD contested. I reject the rider's request to escalate under POL-GEN-26 because the driver's notice is not established: whether the driver notified the rider only bears on POL-RD-24 rows (a) and (b), both of which require a deviation over 1 km. On a 0.60 km deviation row (e) applies whether or not notice was given, so no fact the matrix needs is missing and there is no open question for a human reviewer.\n\nBecause the rider filed and is owed nothing, POL-GEN-03 gives NO_ACTION: the present state stands, the 9.42 SGD metered fare (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.0) is not disturbed, and both money fields are null. The contested amount is 2.00 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, so the AI decides finally; neither profile carries a fraud flag, and POL-RD-25's 0.80 confidence requirement is met. No clause produces a referral."
